\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

\textbf{Research Questions.}
\textbf{RQ1:} Safety--QoE trade-off --- do shields slash aggregate stall while incurring predictable QoE changes vs.\ unconstrained learned policy?\;
\textbf{RQ2:} Baseline competitiveness --- how do constrained \& shield variants align with RobustMPC, Pensieve, heuristics?
\textbf{RQ3:} Ablating Lyapunov/future \& Lagrangian ingredients.

\textbf{Procedure.} Multi-video trace-driven emulator (four evaluation videos, FCC/Norway-style partitioned traces consistent with codebase paths~\cite{fcc2015mba,kvalbein2014}); each episode spans \(K_e{=}48\) chunk decisions with fixed \(T_{\mathrm{c}}\) as in Sec.~\ref{sec:system}; deterministic evaluation policies; Pensieve reproduced with observation masking for fairness.
\textbf{Table~\ref{tab:main:results}} summarizes 80 paired episodes (\(4\times20\)) aggregated means from policy-mode harness logs (exported CSV in the artifact repository beside the plotting script). Companion scripts regenerate publication PDF/PNG figures and excerpt \LaTeX{} table fragments bundled under \texttt{new/src/paper/}.

\textbf{Reporting integrity.} Genie~\cite{mao2017neural} leverages non-causal perfect trace knowledge and should be interpreted informational upper-ish reference --- not deployable parity.

